Executive Summary 


A Business Email Compromise (BEC) incident was investigated involving the Microsoft 365 account of 
Natasha Romanenko. Audit logs identified successful logins from Switzerland, despite the user 
residing in Melbourne and having no history of overseas travel or VPN usage. 
Following authentication, the threat actor accessed SharePoint resources, viewed and downloaded files, and used the compromised mailbox to facilitate a fraudulent payment request sent to ACME Pty Ltd. 


